speechtext:
Please see attached.
a) and b) On March 30, 1990 out of about 120,000 payments made there were 1,608 producers whose payment exceeded the amount which they were actually eligible for under the program. The following is a break-down of that number by reason for overpayment:
i)	1,320 due to a change in yield data supplied by the provincial Crop Insurance Agencies between the time of the interim and the final payment;
ii)	17 due to a failure to correctly cross-reference application and certification forms;
iii)	44 due to processing errors within the program administration;
iv)	55 due to errors made by producers on their application forms;
172 due to the fact that producer payments were less than what had been received under the greenfeed program (50 percent of payments made under the greenfeed program were deducted from CCDAP payments).
